WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.458 --> 00:00:01.510
Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:04.621
Today's message is follow
your intuitive nature.

00:00:04.621 --> 00:00:06.409
Over to you, Phil Jackson.

00:00:06.409 --> 00:00:08.180
(rooster crowing)

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:11.288
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:00:11.288 --> 00:00:14.168
♫ Espresso keep me going.

00:00:14.168 --> 00:00:17.755
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:00:17.755 --> 00:00:19.749
- Who was it, Indy Jones?

00:00:19.749 --> 00:00:23.989
Who's in one of his Indiana
Jones, one of his films,

00:00:23.989 --> 00:00:26.736
Steven Spielberg was asked,

00:00:26.736 --> 00:00:27.797
"What are we going to do next?"

00:00:27.797 --> 00:00:30.809
And he says, " I don't know,
I'm just going by feel here."

00:00:30.809 --> 00:00:34.708
And that's kind of the way it is at times

00:00:34.708 --> 00:00:39.068
that you have to follow
your intuitive nature.

00:00:39.068 --> 00:00:41.889
You don't learn leadership
skills, I think,

00:00:41.889 --> 00:00:42.969
from other people.

00:00:42.969 --> 00:00:45.960
I've gotten a lot of books
sent to me about leadership.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.107
I think management

00:00:48.107 --> 00:00:52.489
has loads of books about
leadership that people read.

00:00:52.489 --> 00:00:55.961
And they can pick up ideas from those.

00:00:55.961 --> 00:00:59.499
But if you're not authentic
or who you really are.

00:00:59.499 --> 00:01:01.716
People see through that pretty quickly.

00:01:01.716 --> 00:01:04.398
- You never have the perfect
information to make a decision.

00:01:04.398 --> 00:01:06.015
This is one of the
challenges of leadership.

00:01:06.015 --> 00:01:09.799
You will never have
complete, 100% information

00:01:09.799 --> 00:01:11.669
to make an important decision.

00:01:11.669 --> 00:01:13.446
Because by the time you get 100%,

00:01:13.446 --> 00:01:15.348
the opportunity will have passed.

00:01:15.348 --> 00:01:17.318
The solution would've already come

00:01:17.318 --> 00:01:19.180
and likely from somebody else.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:21.418
Somebody else is chasing
down that opportunity

00:01:21.418 --> 00:01:23.380
and proved that it works.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:24.840
Where if you don't jump on it

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:26.349
and prove it yourself,

00:01:26.349 --> 00:01:27.885
you're going to lose every time.

00:01:27.885 --> 00:01:29.830
How do you make that
decision when you're only 65,

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:31.913
75, 85 percent confident?

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:34.590
It's by listening to your intuition.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:37.041
You already know what is
the right thing to do.

00:01:37.041 --> 00:01:40.139
Both from a human prospective
of what's right for you

00:01:40.139 --> 00:01:41.309
so that you don't live with regret.

00:01:41.309 --> 00:01:43.718
That this is something
that has to come up.

00:01:43.718 --> 00:01:44.721
And with more experience

00:01:44.721 --> 00:01:46.559
and more practice of
following your intuition.

00:01:46.559 --> 00:01:48.547
You realize what is right for the market,

00:01:48.547 --> 00:01:49.380
what people want,

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:51.496
what is likely to work out or not.

00:01:51.496 --> 00:01:54.365
When I make a new video, for this channel,

00:01:54.365 --> 00:01:55.198
I have an intuitive sense

00:01:55.198 --> 00:01:57.258
of if it's going to be really good or not.

00:01:57.258 --> 00:01:58.780
If I really, really deep down

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:01.527
feel like this is insanely amazing,

00:02:01.527 --> 00:02:04.528
I haven't had many of those videos flop.

00:02:04.528 --> 00:02:05.649
And it comes from experience.

00:02:05.649 --> 00:02:08.418
And the more you hone in on
listening to your intuition,

00:02:08.418 --> 00:02:10.708
the better you're going to get as a leader

00:02:10.708 --> 00:02:12.049
and as an entrepreneur.

00:02:12.049 --> 00:02:13.827
Let me tell you a quick story about Alex,

00:02:13.827 --> 00:02:15.807
who helps me run Toronto Dance Salsa.

00:02:15.807 --> 00:02:17.857
He desperately wanted
to be a better leader.

00:02:17.857 --> 00:02:19.465
When he first joined me last year,

00:02:19.465 --> 00:02:21.598
one of the things he
had to work through was

00:02:21.598 --> 00:02:24.158
he was afraid of confrontation.

00:02:24.158 --> 00:02:26.886
Any time there was a difficult decision,

00:02:26.886 --> 00:02:27.917
potential confrontation,

00:02:27.917 --> 00:02:28.959
he would run away.

00:02:28.959 --> 00:02:29.900
He would delay.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:30.790
He wouldn't write back to you.

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:31.999
He would avoid the situation.

00:02:31.999 --> 00:02:34.087
And by recognizing that
this was something that

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:35.777
he wanted to get better at

00:02:35.777 --> 00:02:39.399
and that he was holding
himself back, subconsciously,

00:02:39.399 --> 00:02:41.738
we slowly worked on getting better.

00:02:41.738 --> 00:02:43.165
When there was an issue that came up,

00:02:43.165 --> 00:02:46.487
he had to convince himself
by thinking it through

00:02:46.487 --> 00:02:49.061
that the behavior I'm doing

00:02:49.061 --> 00:02:50.662
is not rational.

00:02:50.662 --> 00:02:51.987
It's not what I want to do.

00:02:51.987 --> 00:02:53.606
It's not in my own self interest.

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:55.275
It's not in the interest of
the other people, for sure.

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:56.927
But it's not what I want to be doing.

00:02:56.927 --> 00:02:59.548
And so, after thinking
it through for an hour,

00:02:59.548 --> 00:03:02.456
he would get to the point where
he would take action on it.

00:03:02.456 --> 00:03:05.016
Recognizing it was just a fear that he had

00:03:05.016 --> 00:03:06.183
and he slowly got better at it.

00:03:06.183 --> 00:03:08.405
And that one hour became 45 minutes,

00:03:08.405 --> 00:03:09.318
became half an hour,

00:03:09.318 --> 00:03:10.226
became 15 minutes,

00:03:10.226 --> 00:03:12.175
and slowly got to the point where

00:03:12.175 --> 00:03:14.507
when there was a difficult situation,

00:03:14.507 --> 00:03:16.057
he would want to deal with it.

00:03:16.057 --> 00:03:17.288
He would still be afraid

00:03:17.288 --> 00:03:18.397
but he would want to deal with it.

00:03:18.397 --> 00:03:20.208
But it wasn't instinctive yet.

00:03:20.208 --> 00:03:22.065
His instinct was to run away.

00:03:22.065 --> 00:03:23.274
And we all have these things, right?

00:03:23.274 --> 00:03:25.418
We all have these fears,
these insecurities,

00:03:25.418 --> 00:03:26.722
where the instinct is to run away,

00:03:26.722 --> 00:03:27.555
to not address it,

00:03:27.555 --> 00:03:28.421
to not deal with it.

00:03:28.421 --> 00:03:29.531
That was his instinct.

00:03:29.531 --> 00:03:31.961
But because he built a muscle

00:03:31.961 --> 00:03:35.057
and it was in his own best
interest of what he wanted to do,

00:03:35.057 --> 00:03:37.341
how he saw himself as a leader,

00:03:37.341 --> 00:03:39.909
it got more and more and more intuitive

00:03:39.909 --> 00:03:41.318
and more instinctive for him.

00:03:41.318 --> 00:03:44.440
To the point where last
week, at his condo,

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:46.870
there was a fight that
happened downstairs.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:48.428
Two guys broke out into a fight

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:50.839
and nobody was doing anything.

00:03:50.839 --> 00:03:52.397
And now it's not on him to do anything.

00:03:52.397 --> 00:03:55.491
Security guards, right there,
they're not doing anything.

00:03:55.491 --> 00:03:57.794
Nobody wanted to be a leader and step up.

00:03:57.794 --> 00:03:59.491
And the test of a real leader

00:03:59.491 --> 00:04:01.628
is when there is a vacuum of leadership.

00:04:01.628 --> 00:04:03.192
When there is no leadership,

00:04:03.192 --> 00:04:06.490
a leader steps in and fills the void.

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:10.720
And so Alex, didn't take
an hour to think about it,

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:13.319
he jumped in and he stopped the fight.

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:16.347
He did what the best
version of himself would do.

00:04:16.347 --> 00:04:18.264
And it was an instinct.

00:04:18.264 --> 00:04:20.949
He managed to take the thing
that he was not good at,

00:04:20.949 --> 00:04:22.429
it was the opposite of,

00:04:22.429 --> 00:04:23.869
he would run away from every situation

00:04:23.869 --> 00:04:26.526
that was potentially
having conflict in it.

00:04:26.526 --> 00:04:28.388
To the point where it came
something that he thought about

00:04:28.388 --> 00:04:29.349
and slowly fixed.

00:04:29.349 --> 00:04:30.908
To the point where now it's his instinct

00:04:30.908 --> 00:04:33.478
and his habit to jump in
and solve the problem.

00:04:33.478 --> 00:04:34.939
With experience of understanding

00:04:34.939 --> 00:04:37.647
where you are limiting yourself,

00:04:37.647 --> 00:04:40.849
what behaviors you are doing
that are holding yourself back,

00:04:40.849 --> 00:04:43.407
and with repeated effort and
practice to build the muscle,

00:04:43.407 --> 00:04:46.569
through practice, through
dedication, through continuance,

00:04:46.569 --> 00:04:48.709
you can get to the point

00:04:48.709 --> 00:04:50.866
where that behavior that
you wanted to change,

00:04:50.866 --> 00:04:51.699
that you would run away from,

00:04:51.699 --> 00:04:55.567
now becomes an instinctive
reaction to do the right thing.

00:04:55.567 --> 00:04:59.596
The more you follow your
intuition and lean in on it,

00:04:59.596 --> 00:05:01.357
the more you practice doing the thing

00:05:01.357 --> 00:05:04.386
that the best version of you wants to do,

00:05:04.386 --> 00:05:07.707
then the closer you will
close the gap for yourself

00:05:07.707 --> 00:05:08.938
and make the right decisions

00:05:08.938 --> 00:05:11.016
and have the biggest impact that you can.

00:05:11.016 --> 00:05:12.977
So the question day
today is that I'm curious

00:05:12.977 --> 00:05:15.866
what was the last instinctive
decision that you made

00:05:15.866 --> 00:05:18.316
that turned out really well for you?

00:05:18.316 --> 00:05:20.319
Where you didn't have complete information

00:05:20.319 --> 00:05:22.600
but you made a gut check and it worked.

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:23.459
Let me know.

00:05:23.459 --> 00:05:24.609
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:05:24.609 --> 00:05:26.167
I'm super curious to find out.

00:05:26.167 --> 00:05:28.350
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Lim Kee Sitt.

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:30.508
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:05:30.508 --> 00:05:31.589
Your One Word.

00:05:31.589 --> 00:05:33.097
I really, really appreciate the support.

00:05:33.097 --> 00:05:34.268
I hope you're learning from the book

00:05:34.268 --> 00:05:35.467
and you're applying it to your life

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:36.657
and to your business.

00:05:36.657 --> 00:05:37.800
Thank you, guys, again, for watching.

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:39.517
I hope you have an amazing day.

00:05:39.517 --> 00:05:40.568
I believe in you

00:05:40.568 --> 00:05:42.969
and hope you continue
to believe in yourself.

00:05:42.969 --> 00:05:44.164
And I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:05:44.164 --> 00:05:46.666
for another shot of Inspesso.

00:05:46.666 --> 00:05:49.369
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:05:49.369 --> 00:05:52.869
♫ Espresso keep me going.

00:05:55.345 --> 00:05:56.718
Well I left college because

00:05:56.718 --> 00:05:59.397
I knew exactly what I wanted to do

00:05:59.397 --> 00:06:02.093
and some of you know, too.

00:06:02.093 --> 00:06:04.174
But some of you don't.

00:06:04.174 --> 00:06:05.544
Or maybe you thought you knew

00:06:05.544 --> 00:06:08.264
but are now questioning that choice.

00:06:08.264 --> 00:06:09.903
Maybe you're sitting
there trying to figure out

00:06:09.903 --> 00:06:11.571
how to tell your parents

00:06:11.571 --> 00:06:13.092
that you want to be a doctor

00:06:13.092 --> 00:06:14.780
and not a comedy writer.

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:17.030
(laughing)

00:06:18.053 --> 00:06:19.653
Well, what you choose to do next

00:06:19.653 --> 00:06:21.171
is what we call, in the movies,

00:06:21.171 --> 00:06:23.673
the character defining moment.

00:06:23.673 --> 00:06:25.614
Now these are moments
you're very familiar with.

00:06:25.614 --> 00:06:28.613
Like, in the last Star
Wars: The Force Awakens,

00:06:28.613 --> 00:06:32.183
when Rey realizes the Force is with her,

00:06:32.183 --> 00:06:34.624
or Indiana Jones choosing
mission over fear

00:06:34.624 --> 00:06:37.123
by jumping into a pile of snakes.

00:06:37.123 --> 00:06:39.471
Now in a two hour movie,

00:06:39.471 --> 00:06:42.103
you get a handful of
character defining moments.

00:06:42.103 --> 00:06:45.700
But in real life, you face them every day.

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:48.283
Life is one strong, long string

00:06:49.603 --> 00:06:51.235
of character defining moments.

00:06:51.235 --> 00:06:53.594
And I was lucky that, at 18,

00:06:53.594 --> 00:06:56.282
I knew what I exactly wanted to do.

00:06:56.282 --> 00:06:58.615
But I didn't know who I was.

00:07:01.904 --> 00:07:03.151
How could I?

00:07:03.151 --> 00:07:04.084
And how could any of us?

00:07:04.084 --> 00:07:06.943
Because for the first
25 years of our lives,

00:07:06.943 --> 00:07:11.363
we are trained to listen to
voices that are not our own.

00:07:11.363 --> 00:07:13.204
Parents and professors fill up our heads

00:07:13.204 --> 00:07:15.015
with wisdom and information

00:07:15.015 --> 00:07:17.882
and then employers and
mentors take their place

00:07:17.882 --> 00:07:21.753
and explain how this world really works.

00:07:21.753 --> 00:07:23.717
And usually these voices
of authority make sense

00:07:23.717 --> 00:07:27.612
but sometimes, doubt starts
to creep in our heads

00:07:27.612 --> 00:07:28.633
and into our hearts

00:07:28.633 --> 00:07:30.891
and even when we think,

00:07:30.891 --> 00:07:33.701
that's not quite how I see the world,

00:07:33.701 --> 00:07:37.062
it's kind of easier just to
nod and agree and go along.

00:07:37.062 --> 00:07:42.023
And for a while I let that
going along define my character.

00:07:42.023 --> 00:07:45.543
Because I was repressing
my own point of view

00:07:45.543 --> 00:07:47.711
because like in that Nillson song,

00:07:47.711 --> 00:07:49.341
everybody was talking at me

00:07:49.341 --> 00:07:52.320
so I couldn't hear the echoes of my mind.

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:56.111
And, at first, the internal
voice I needed to listen to

00:07:56.111 --> 00:07:58.932
was hardly audible and
it was hardly noticeable.

00:07:58.932 --> 00:08:01.202
Kind of like me in high school.

00:08:01.202 --> 00:08:04.081
But then I started paying more attention

00:08:04.081 --> 00:08:06.331
and my intuition kicked in.

00:08:07.262 --> 00:08:09.222
And I want to be clear that your intuition

00:08:09.222 --> 00:08:11.678
is different from your conscience.

00:08:11.678 --> 00:08:13.941
They work in tandem, but
here's the distinction.

00:08:13.941 --> 00:08:18.881
Your conscience shouts,
"Here's what you should do!"

00:08:18.881 --> 00:08:23.371
While your intuition whispers,
"Here's what you could do."

00:08:23.371 --> 00:08:27.150
Listen to that voice that
tells you what you could do.

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:31.762
Nothing will define your
character more than that.

00:08:31.762 --> 00:08:34.759
Because once I turned to my intuition

00:08:34.759 --> 00:08:36.426
and I tuned into it,

00:08:38.110 --> 00:08:40.833
certain projects began
to pull me into them

00:08:40.833 --> 00:08:42.870
and others I turned away from.

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:44.800
- Now why did you decide
to come out with Roar?

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:46.292
There was that big countdown

00:08:46.292 --> 00:08:47.380
and then Roar came out

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:48.501
and it was huge for you.

00:08:48.501 --> 00:08:50.153
I mean, you broke your own records there.

00:08:50.153 --> 00:08:52.353
Why wasn't Roar the first single?

00:08:52.353 --> 00:08:54.750
- Um, you know, it was up for debate.

00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:59.072
A couple of singles, it was
going to be Roar or another one

00:08:59.072 --> 00:09:01.722
and we decided to go with Roar

00:09:01.722 --> 00:09:04.651
because of the reaction I
was getting from my friends.

00:09:04.651 --> 00:09:07.818
I kind of use my friends as Guinea pigs.

00:09:08.731 --> 00:09:10.032
As test Guinea pigs.

00:09:10.032 --> 00:09:13.100
And I have a very
eclectic group of friends

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:16.683
ranging from DJs, to
artists, to just moms.

00:09:18.919 --> 00:09:23.086
And they all really agreed
that Roar was the best one.

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:27.229
And it has that bouncy feel,

00:09:27.229 --> 00:09:28.852
that eighth note feel,

00:09:28.852 --> 00:09:30.782
but it also has this message of

00:09:30.782 --> 00:09:32.561
finding your inner strength again

00:09:32.561 --> 00:09:34.871
and letting that, kind
of, come out as a roar.

00:09:34.871 --> 00:09:36.561
And people related to it.

00:09:36.561 --> 00:09:37.609
- Yeah, well they really did.

00:09:37.609 --> 00:09:39.398
- And there's something,
yeah, there's something,

00:09:39.398 --> 00:09:41.899
like there's an intuitive thing
that happens inside of me.

00:09:41.899 --> 00:09:44.914
And I always trust my
intuition when it comes to

00:09:44.914 --> 00:09:47.044
writing songs and picking which songs

00:09:47.044 --> 00:09:48.939
should come out as singles.

00:09:48.939 --> 00:09:50.312
- You fall in love with somebody here,

00:09:50.312 --> 00:09:51.960
you don't love them here, what happens?

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:53.220
You get a stomach ache here.

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:54.793
Where do you fall in love?

00:09:54.793 --> 00:09:55.780
With your stomach.

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:58.030
(laughing)

00:10:01.367 --> 00:10:04.477
Are you cultivating your intuition?

00:10:04.477 --> 00:10:05.631
And I would say,

00:10:05.631 --> 00:10:07.819
if you're not drinking
enough beer at The Oasis,

00:10:07.819 --> 00:10:09.900
you're not taking advantage
of your education.

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:11.068
(laughing)

00:10:11.068 --> 00:10:12.451
Because what you're going to do in life,

00:10:12.451 --> 00:10:14.109
is you're always going
to be gaging people,

00:10:14.109 --> 00:10:15.531
if they're BSers or not.

00:10:15.531 --> 00:10:18.271
And if you're not cultivating
your human skills,

00:10:18.271 --> 00:10:20.089
They're going to snow ya.

00:10:20.089 --> 00:10:20.922
You know what I mean?

00:10:20.922 --> 00:10:22.439
Drinking beer is not your enemy.

00:10:22.439 --> 00:10:24.500
Drinking beer and
socializing, having coffee,

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:27.722
you're learning that those
are very constructive moments.

00:10:27.722 --> 00:10:29.379
You're learning, is that a person a BSer?

00:10:29.379 --> 00:10:30.659
Or can I trust them?

00:10:30.659 --> 00:10:34.203
What is the behavior that I
really want from my workers?

